  "name": "Runeword: Zelkar, the Hungry Void",
  "type": "feat",
  "effects": [],
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "gm": "",
      "value": "<p style=\"border:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext .75pt;padding:0in;mso-padding-alt:0in 0in 1.0pt 0in\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><strong>Prerequisites</strong> Runescribe dedication</p><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><strong>Requirements</strong> You have prepared spells in your three highest ranked spell slots that you have not cast and you have Farum inscribed on your person.</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><strong>Frequency</strong> Once per hour</p><hr></div><p class=\"MsoNormal\">You invoke Zelkar to draw upon one element of your magic, converting it to another usable form of ether. You select a spell that meets the requirements. That spell slot becomes burnt, and Farum becomes charged and you gain a focus point. If you consume a spell from your highest ranked spell slots, you gain two focus points instead.</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">If you have the @UUID[Compendium.immortal-ardor.archetypes.HgwLIRVq8nWEBQJn]{Fragmentary Runes} feat, you can sacrifice a fragmentary rune for 1 focus point when you use this action instead of a spell slot.</p>"
